    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0465" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/2–953: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-02-09T19:14:00-05:00">February 9,
                            1953—7:14 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>493. Re items on GA agenda.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>4. The appointment of a secretary general seems to me a particularly delicate
                    negotiating problem. The alternatives seem to be whether there can be agreement
                    on a new secretary general satisfactory to us or whether there must be an acting
                    secretary general appointed by the Assembly. It is too early to say which
                    solution will occur and precisely how to go about seeing to it that an
                    individual satisfactory to us is finally agreed upon. At this time, however, I
                    see disadvantages in the US joining any active group in promoting any particular
                    candidate.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lodge</hi>
                        </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
